{%- comment -%}
  BMP curated-first — standalone single-card section.

  Fetched by assets/bmp-curated-first.js via the Section Rendering API:
    /products/{handle}?section_id=bmp-curated-product-card
  when the clicked product is NOT already in the visited collection grid.

  Renders the card content (image, title, price) DIRECTLY instead of
  delegating to a static `_product-card` block via the "render this section's
  configured block" liquid tag. That tag resolves a static block's CHILD
  blocks from the section's `blocks{}`/`block_order[]` configuration in a
  template's JSON — but this section is never placed in any template (it
  exists only to be invoked via the Section Rendering API), so it has zero
  configured child blocks and that delegating call used to render nothing: an
  empty, still-clickable `<li>` shell (the CRITICAL bug this rewrite fixes).
  Native precedent: sections/section-rendering-product-card.liquid —
  Horizon's own SRA-only card (used by quick-add / variant-picker morphing) —
  avoids that same delegation for exactly this reason and renders its markup
  inline.

  Not pixel-identical to a merchant-configured `_product-card` block — no
  badges, swatches, or per-card layout settings, since those live on block
  instances this section doesn't have — but it reuses the SAME classes and
  custom elements the real cards render (`.product-card`,
  `.product-card__link`, `.card-gallery`, `.product-media-container`,
  `.text-block`, `<product-price>`) so it (a) inherits the shared card
  title/price typography lock in assets/bmp-styles.css and (b) stays a valid
  target for assets/bmp-curated-first.js's own selectors (setVariantOnLinks
  rewrites every anchor pointing at this product; swapImage looks for
  `.card-gallery img` / `.product-media-container img` — see that file's
  header comment).

  The outer `<li class="product-grid__item" ref="cards[]">` wrapper stays
  byte-compatible with the items sections/main-collection.liquid emits so
  the JS can slot this straight into the grid at position #1. `data-page`
  below is only a placeholder default: assets/bmp-curated-first.js's
  moveToFront() overwrites it with the page number of the card this one
  displaces, so upward infinite-scroll pagination keeps resolving the correct
  "previous page" from cards[0].dataset.page (assets/paginated-list.js).
  That overwrite only became real on 2026-08-04 — it previously read
  `grid.firstElementChild`, which on the storefront is the sessionStorage
  grid-view <script> from snippets/product-grid.liquid:141-166 rather than a
  card, so the stamp silently never ran in production while still firing in
  the theme editor (where that script is not rendered). Do not reintroduce a
  `firstElementChild` lookup here or in that file.

  LAYOUT CONTRACT (code review 2026-08-04). Reusing the real cards' CLASSES is
  not enough: three of Horizon's card layout inputs are custom properties that
  only ever exist as INLINE styles on the server-rendered cards, so a card that
  omits them gets an invalid declaration and silently falls back to the CSS
  initial value —
    --gallery-aspect-ratio  emitted only at snippets/card-gallery.liquid:91.
      snippets/product-media-container-styles.liquid:13 is
      `aspect-ratio: var(--gallery-aspect-ratio, var(--media-preview-ratio))`,
      and --media-preview-ratio exists only on PDP gallery markup (never on
      :root), so with neither set the whole declaration is invalid at
      computed-value time and the media box falls back to `aspect-ratio: auto`.
    --product-media-fit  + the `media-fit` class, both set at
      snippets/card-gallery.liquid:123,134 — without them there is no crop.
    --product-card-gap  emitted only by the inline `gap-style` render at
      snippets/product-card.liquid:106. snippets/product-card-styles.liquid:13
      is `gap: var(--product-card-gap)` with NO fallback, so an unset var
      computes `gap: normal` and the title/price sit higher than on siblings.
  The values below mirror what templates/collection.json ships today
  (`image_ratio: "square"` -> ratio `1`, `product_card_gap: 4`). They are the
  FLOOR, not the whole fix: assets/bmp-curated-first.js copies the class+style
  of a sibling real card onto this one before insertion whenever the grid has
  one, so a merchant changing those settings still gets a matching card. The
  inline values are what keeps the card correct in the case the copy cannot
  cover — an empty or fully-filtered grid, which is precisely when the SRA
  fallback path runs.

  `product` is the page product (this section is only ever fetched on a
  /products/{handle} URL).
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign url = product.url
  assign featured_media = product.featured_media
%}
{%- if product == blank or product.id == blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Unknown, unpublished or draft handle. Shopify still answers the Section
    Rendering API with HTTP 200 here and a nil `product`, so rendering the card
    anyway produced an <li> with href="" that assets/bmp-curated-first.js could
    never match against the requested handle — which is what let pin()
    re-insert a clone every animation frame.

    Render nothing instead: fetchAndPin() treats a card-less body as a failed
    lookup, warns once, and no-ops.
  {%- endcomment -%}
{%- else -%}
{% # theme-check-disable ValidScopedCSSClass %}
<li
  id="bmp-curated-{{ product.id }}"
  class="product-grid__item product-grid__item--0"
  data-page="1"
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  data-bmp-curated-pin="true"
  ref="cards[]"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    Card-global-style carrier. `display: contents` in
    assets/bmp-styles.css, so it is layout-inert — but NOT selector-inert, and
    that is exactly why it has to be here: the global Card group is scoped as
    `.bmp-card-global-card div.product-card__content`, an ANCESTOR class, and
    assets/bmp-curated-first.js `adoptSiblingLayout()` copies class and style
    node-to-node for `.product-card__content` / `.card-gallery` /
    `.product-media-container` only. An ancestor cannot be copied, so without
    this line the global gap/background/border/radius/padding would never reach
    this card in EITHER path — not just the sibling-less one. Media is fine
    without it, since `bmp-card-global-media` rides the `.card-gallery` copy.

    Emitted unconditionally, on the same footing as the hardcoded
    `--product-card-gap: 4px` and `--gallery-aspect-ratio: 1` below: it mirrors
    what templates/collection.json ships, which is the toggle ON for the
    `_product-card` wrapper. adoptSiblingLayout() corrects it against a live
    sibling before insertion, so a merchant who turns the toggle off still gets
    a matching card; the unconditional value is the floor for the case the copy
    cannot cover.

    The inner markup deliberately keeps its indentation — re-indenting eighty
    lines to add one wrapper would bury the change.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="bmp-card-global-card">
  <product-card
    class="product-card"
    data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
    {% # theme-check-disable UnknownFilter %}
    view-event-payload="{{ product | standard_event_data: 'view', context: 'collection' | escape }}"
    {% # theme-check-enable UnknownFilter %}
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      The `id` here is LOAD-BEARING, not decorative — do not drop it as
      cosmetic. assets/product-card.js:572 (`navigateToProduct`) reads
      `link.getAttribute('id')` and early-returns when it is absent, BEFORE it
      reaches `#navigateToURL` at :592. The absolute `inset: 0` overlay does
      not cover for that: `.product-card` is a stacking context
      (assets/base.css:104-108) and inside it `.product-card__content`
      (relative) paints over `.product-card__link` (absolute, z-index auto), so
      the content box is the hit target everywhere there is no anchor — which
      is why Horizon routes those clicks through JS in the first place. Without
      an id the price row and the space beside the title do nothing.

      Namespaced rather than mirroring the real card's
      `'product-card-link-' | append: block.id | append: '-' | append: product.id`
      (snippets/product-card.liquid:35,82): this section has no `block.id` to
      mirror, and a distinct prefix also guarantees no duplicate DOM id during
      the window where this clone and the genuine server-rendered card are both
      in the grid, before findOtherCardWithHandle() swaps them.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <a
      id="{{ 'bmp-curated-' | append: product.id | md5 }}"
      class="product-card__link"
      ref="productCardLink"
      href="{{ url }}"
      aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}"
    ></a>
    <div
      class="product-card__content layout-panel-flex layout-panel-flex--column product-grid__card spacing-style border-style gap-style"
      style="--product-card-gap: 4px;"
    >
      <div
        class="card-gallery"
        ref="cardGallery"
        style="--gallery-aspect-ratio: 1;"
        data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
      >
        {%- if featured_media -%}
          <a class="contents" ref="cardGalleryLink" href="{{ url }}" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}">
            <div class="product-media-container media-fit" style="--product-media-fit: cover;">
              {%- comment -%}
                `eager`, not `lazy`. snippets/card-gallery.liquid:112-118 makes
                every server-rendered card in the grid eager whenever
                `section.index < 5`, and main-collection is well inside that in
                templates/collection.json. This card is grid slot #1 by
                construction, so shipping it lazy made the ad's own product the
                LAST image to appear on the ad landing — behind the deferred
                low-priority module AND the Section Rendering API round trip.
                assets/bmp-curated-first.js additionally sets fetchPriority on
                the node before insertion. Both together raise the floor; they
                do not make this competitive with a server-rendered hero, which
                is what a server-side pin would buy.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {{
                featured_media
                | image_url: width: 700
                | image_tag:
                  loading: 'eager',
                  alt: featured_media.alt | default: product.title,
                  sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 25vw, 50vw',
                  widths: '240, 352, 480, 640, 832, 1200, 1600, 1920'
              }}
            </div>
          </a>
        {%- else -%}
          <a class="contents" ref="cardGalleryLink" href="{{ url }}">
            <span class="title-text">{{ product.title }}</span>
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      <div class="text-block">
        <a class="contents" href="{{ url }}">{{ product.title }}</a>
      </div>
      <product-price>
        {% render 'price', product_resource: product, show_unit_price: true %}
      </product-price>
    </div>
  </product-card>
  </div>
</li>
{% # theme-check-enable ValidScopedCSSClass %}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "BMP: Curated card",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
